---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const latest = "https://github.com/ABorakati/zotero-next/releases/latest";
---
<Site page="download" title="Download" description="Download the Zotero Next installer for Windows 10 and 11, and set up the Word add-in and the browser connector.">
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="wrap slip-wrap">
			<div>
				<h1 class="display" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem">Take it home</h1>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 2rem">One installer for the app, the Word add-in and the browser connector. It installs for your Windows user only and never changes your Zotero library.</p>
				<div class="actions">
					<a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={latest}><Icon name="download" />Download 0.1.0 from GitHub</a>
					<a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href={`${base}user-guide/install/`}><Icon name="book-open" />Install guide</a>
				</div>
				<p class="fine" style="margin-top: 1.25rem">The repository is private: the link works when you are signed in to GitHub with access to it.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="slip" data-reveal>
				<h3>Date due</h3>
				<table>
					<tbody>
						<tr style="--r:0"><td>Needs</td><td>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit</td></tr>
						<tr style="--r:1"><td>Installs to</td><td>your user, no admin</td></tr>
						<tr style="--r:2"><td>Size</td><td>about 145 MB</td></tr>
						<tr style="--r:3"><td>Updates</td><td>signed auto-update</td></tr>
						<tr style="--r:4"><td>Released</td><td class="typed-date">7 Nov 2026</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="room" style="background: var(--ground-2)">
		<div class="wrap volume" style="align-items: start">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom: 1.1rem">Install</h2>
				<p>The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen says the publisher is unknown. Click <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>.</p>
				<p>Your installed copy lives in <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Zotero Next</code>. Uninstalling removes the program, never a library.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<div class="card-head"><span>ZN 0.1.0</span><span>Installing</span></div>
				<ol class="card-steps">
					<li><div><strong>Run the installer.</strong><p>Pick the parts you want. Close Word first if you install the add-in.</p></div></li>
					<li><div><strong>Choose a library.</strong><p>Import from Zotero (only read), open a Zotero Next library, or start empty. <a href={`${base}user-guide/first-run/`}>First run</a>.</p></div></li>
					<li><div><strong>Pick a sync route.</strong><p>A local Zotero, or zotero.org with or without attachments. <a href={`${base}user-guide/sync/`}>Sync</a>.</p></div></li>
				</ol>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="wrap" style="margin-top: 2.5rem">
			<p class="fine">Silent install, for scripts:</p>
			<pre class="typed">ZoteroNext-Setup-0.1.0.exe /VERYSILENT /SUPPRESSMSGBOXES /NORESTART /COMPONENTS="app,word,connector"</pre>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="room" id="connector">
		<div class="wrap volume" style="align-items: start">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom: 1.1rem">The browser connector</h2>
				<p>The installer registers the helper program. Browsers do not let an installer add an extension, so load it once yourself. It takes about thirty seconds, and afterwards pages save even when Zotero Next is closed.</p>
				<p>The official Zotero Connector also works, but only while the app is open. Keep one connector per browser, or every page shows two Save buttons.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<div class="card-head"><span>ZN 0.1.0</span><span>Connector</span></div>
				<ol class="card-steps">
					<li><div><strong>Open the extensions page.</strong><p><code>chrome://extensions</code> or <code>edge://extensions</code>.</p></div></li>
					<li><div><strong>Turn on Developer mode.</strong></div></li>
					<li><div><strong>Load unpacked.</strong><p>Pick <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Zotero Next\connector\extension</code>.</p></div></li>
					<li><div><strong>Check the ID.</strong><p><code>pakgagonakcalfbmckaolkpidcojacaf</code>, then pin the button.</p></div></li>
				</ol>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="room" style="background: var(--ground-2)">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="ledger">
				<div class="ledger-row">
					<h3><span class="row-icon"><Icon name="file-text" size={18} /></span>Word add-in</h3>
					<p>Insert and edit live citations and a bibliography from a sidebar, even with the app closed.</p>
					<a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href={`${base}user-guide/word/`}>Word add-in guide<Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} /></a>
				</div>
				<div class="ledger-row">
					<h3><span class="row-icon"><Icon name="bot" size={18} /></span>MCP for agents</h3>
					<p>Connect Claude Code or another MCP client to your library and to the open Word document.</p>
					<a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href={`${base}user-guide/mcp/`}>MCP setup<Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} /></a>
				</div>
				<div class="ledger-row">
					<h3><span class="row-icon"><Icon name="hammer" size={18} /></span>Build from source</h3>
					<p>Bun 1.4.4, Rust for the PDF library, and Inno Setup 7 for the installer. No Node or npm.</p>
					<a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href={`${base}developer-guide/building/`}>Building guide<Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} /></a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Site>
